title: ShinyHunters PeopleSoft Intrusion - Staging and Exfiltration Infrastructure
id: 503dd8e3-e0eb-4df3-a33f-9e46eaa3f363
status: experimental
description: >
    Detects network connections to documented ShinyHunters (UNC6240) staging
    and exfiltration infrastructure used in the Oracle PeopleSoft exploitation
    campaign (CVE-2026-35273) that also produced the FBI jobs-portal breach:
    MeshCentral agents on 142.11.200.186-190 masquerading as Azure via
    azurenetfiles.net, zstd-compressed exfiltration over SSH to 176.120.22.24,
    and the 108.174.202.99 host reported in the same campaign.
references:
    - https://cloud.google.com/blog/topics/threat-intelligence/shinyhunters-renewed-mass-exploitation-campaign-targeting-oracle-peoplesoft/
    - https://www.bleepingcomputer.com/news/security/shinyhunters-claims-fbi-hack-data-theft-in-peoplesoft-zero-day-breach/
    - https://www.bleepingcomputer.com/news/security/shinyhunters-uses-waf-bypass-trick-in-oracle-peoplesoft-attacks/
    - https://gbhackers.com/accenture-contractor-removed-after-fbi-data-breach/
author: Tia N. List
date: 2026-10-07
tags:
    - attack.t1190
    - attack.t1048
logsource:
    category: network_connection
    product: windows
detection:
    selection_ip:
        DestinationIp:
            - '142.11.200.186'
            - '142.11.200.187'
            - '142.11.200.188'
            - '142.11.200.189'
            - '142.11.200.190'
            - '176.120.22.24'
            - '108.174.202.99'
    selection_host:
        DestinationHostname|endswith:
            - 'azurenetfiles.net'
    condition: selection_ip or selection_host
falsepositives:
    - Reuse or reassignment of the reported hosting ranges after law enforcement action
    - Rare legitimate MeshCentral or remote-monitoring deployments on the same providers
level: high
